  "question": {
    "text": "If $x^m \\cdot y^n=(x+y)^{m+n}$, then $\\frac{d y}{d x}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ymdYq",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{y}{x}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "YDrVA",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x+y}{x y}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pL7T7",
      "text": "\nxy\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lNvFH",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{y}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x^m \\cdot y^n=(x+y)^{m+n} \\Rightarrow m \\ln x+n \\ln y=(m+n) \\ln (x+y)$\n$\\therefore \\frac{m}{x}+\\frac{n}{y} \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{m+n}{x+y}\\left(1+\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right) \\Rightarrow\\left(\\frac{m}{x}-\\frac{m+n}{x+y}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{m+n}{x+y}-\\frac{n}{y}\\right) \\frac{d y}{d x}$\n$\\quad \\frac{m y-n x}{x(x+y)}=\\left(\\frac{m y-n x}{y(x+y)}\\right) \\frac{d y}{d x} \\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{y}{x}$",
    "image": null
  },
